daemon: Never end a drag because a finger lifted while the click is held

Chris: holding the physical click with one finger and dragging with another,
lifting the moving finger to reposition (the selection reaches the screen edge)
ended the selection. DragDebug log from pkgrel 14:

  fw-bit-down at 3018 ms, BTN_LEFT-down, latch at 3185 ms (2 contacts),
  contacts 2 -> 1 at 3817 ms, drag-end "drag contact lifted while other contacts
  remain", BTN_LEFT-up at 3817 ms, fw-bit-up only at 5066 ms.

The firmware button bit was held for 1.2 s more, but the latch treated the
lifted drag contact as the end of the drag whenever another contact remained
(the resting click finger), and released BTN_LEFT.

While the firmware button bit is held, a lifted drag contact now never ends the
drag or releases BTN_LEFT:

 - The drag stays latched. Tracking moves to the newest contact (a newly placed
   finger, else the remaining one); with no contact left it waits for one.
   Contacts are passed through unchanged, so pointer motion continues from the
   new finger without a jump.
 - A drag that was waiting for the finger (DragRelatchMs) and sees the bit
   pressed again keeps going instead of timing out.
 - Once the bit is released the existing rules apply again: the drag contact
   lifted -> wait DragRelatchMs / release, or the stillness timer -> park ->
   release. Without a physical click (bit low: tap and drag, parked drag) nothing
   changes.

DragDebug logs the new path: "drag-keep" (contact lifted but firmware button
still held) once per lift, and "drag-keep-handoff" when tracking moved to
another contact.

